  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">00140944 SDG FUNDS Joint Programming: Sustainable Transformation of Municipal Markets in Panama: Circular Economy and Zero Waste</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">This project aims to revolutionize waste management and promote circular economy practices in Panama City&#x2019;s municipal markets, contributing significantly to sustainable development. By implementing advanced organic waste management systems and food rescue programs, the initiative targets a 10% reduction in waste sent to landfills and a 150-kilo monthly compost production, directly supporting SDG 12 (Responsible Consumption and Production) and SDG 2 (Zero Hunger).</narrative>
  </description>
